# jAER progress reports

Canonical handoff notes live in the **jAER repo**:

`.cursor/progress-reports/<short_name>.md`

(e.g. `usb_open_hang.md`). That folder Dropbox-syncs across machines. Gitignores those `*.md` files; that is fine.

Plans (`.cursor/plans/*.plan.md`) are the intended design. Progress reports are **where we left off** after messy, multi-file, human-in-the-loop work. Do not substitute one for the other.

## When to write

Write or update a report when **all** of these hold:

- Substantial debugging, or implementing a new feature
- Many files (or a wide live path: USB, ViewLoop, filters, render, chips)
- Needs the user's interaction, log inspection, or manual testing (`ant run`, hardware, UI)

Skip one-file fixes, compile errors, Q&A, and work that finishes in the same turn.

## When to read

At the start of a session, if this folder has a report that matches the current task, **read it before** searching or editing. Prefer the report over guessing from chat (chat does not Dropbox-sync).

## What to put in the file

Keep it short and current. Overwrite stale sections; do not append a diary.

- **Aim** — what we are trying to fix or ship
- **Status** — done / in progress / blocked
- **Touched** — key files, not a dump
- **How to test** — what the user was running, logs to check (`jAER-0.log`, usb-open-trace)
- **Next** — the immediate next step on this or another box
- **Blockers** — waiting on hardware, a log, a decision

Update after each substantial turn, and **before stopping** so the other machine has a complete handoff.

## Do

- One file per task; descriptive name (`usb_autobind_restore.md`), not a timestamp-only name
- Create `.cursor/progress-reports/` if it is missing
- If a Dropbox conflicted copy appears, merge into the canonical filename and delete the conflict file

## Do not

- Write these notes only in chat, `~/.cursor/`, or `%USERPROFILE%\.cursor\`
- Scatter reports under `docs/`, `/tmp`, or random paths unless the user asks
- Create a report for trivial work
